preConditionHook:
// EL: rangeSum over bars 1..lookback of high[kk] - low[kk], divided by
// lookback, and AbsValue(close - open) > bodyMultiple * that mean -- Grimes's
// strong-momentum rejection bar (G05-10), the bar that closes back across a
// broken level.
//
// NOT BodyAboveAverageMultiple, which sizes the body against the mean BODY and
// demands a with-trend colour. This sizes it against the mean RANGE, a much
// harder test at the same multiple, and is direction-agnostic -- both sides are
// identical text.
//
// The benchmark window EXCLUDES the bar it judges (bars 1..lookback), the
// LargeOutsideBar / BodyAboveAverageMultiple convention, so an outsized body
// cannot raise its own benchmark. The mean is an explicit summation rather than
// Average(...)[1]: Average over a price expression with real history is a fresh
// loop, but reading a function call's OWN history at an offset is unmeasured.
// The summation runs newest-first, EasyLanguage's Summation order, and divides
// by the same (int) bound the loop uses.
//
// The accumulator is a class member and persists across bars, so it is reset.
//
// Deepest bar touched: lookback.
rangeSum = 0.0;
for (int i = 1; i <= (int)lookback; ++i) {
    rangeSum = rangeSum + (high[i] - low[i]);
}
avgRange = rangeSum / (int)lookback;
